Z||000000||Haze_Performance||04-24-2000||03:37 AM||||When I start my 2M4 it will idle at just over 2000rpm's untill it warms up (about 5 mins). Then it warms up and its steady at 800rpm. I checked all the vac. lines and there all good, no leaks. I did a complete tune-up and it still does it. Is this a normal Fiero thing?||||reg||1
Z||000001||CUTTER||04-24-2000||03:50 AM||||My car does the same thing but my tach fluxuates........?........anyway, I think its a normal thing, everyone I know that has a fiero (2 people) talks about the same thing or something simular.||||reg||1
Z||000002||gbv||04-24-2000||08:43 AM||||same here. although mine only goes to about 1200-1500rpm till i drive it for a few mins and it settles at the normal 800-900.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||04-24-2000||09:42 AM||||Remove and clean your IAC valve and it's port. This should help bring your cold start idle down to 1000 - 1200 rpm. They get dirty and open a little too much when cold.<BR>Note: be careful not to push and turn the cone shaped tip. This will change its alignment. When you replace it back in the car, it may idle high. This is normal, you will need to drive it over 40mph for the ECM to reset it then idle should be fine.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||04-25-2000||02:51 AM||||Driving over 40 will not be a problem  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Thank Again for the info Guys   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 04-25-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000005||Hawkman||04-25-2000||08:21 AM||||I'm brand new to my 85 Fiero and mine idles at when cold at about 2000 rpm for 30 seconds then settles down to 1000 rpm at idle.  1000 rpm seems too high to me and it never gets below that even when warm.<P>Where is the IAC located and what does it look like?  I'm assuming the IAC is the idle air control - am I right?<P>Thanks tons for the help!||||reg||1
Z||000006||85SE||04-25-2000||03:23 PM||||From what I've gathered from other fiero reading, the correct idle for our cars is around 1000 rpm, but I don't recall if that was specific to either motor or generally.<P>Where is the IAC located and what does it look like?  I'm assuming the IAC is the idle air control - am I right?<P>I haven't quite figured out exactly where the IAC is, but according to my manual it's next to the "Fuel Injector" (looks like TB) on the 4 and to the left of the distributor on the 6.  Sorry that I can't be more specific.<P>The manual also notes that code 35 will be set if idle varies by 50 rpm from correct for longer than 30 seconds.<P><p>[This message has been edited by 85SE (edited 04-25-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Standard||04-26-2000||01:55 AM||||I'm pretty sure that the idle for both the 4 and 6 cyl when warm should be 750 rpm for auto, and 900 rpm for manual.  the high idle on startup is progarammed into the ecm, something that GM thought they needed.  warms up faster or build oil pressure faster or something like that.  please correct me if I'm wrong.. my thinking is not too clear right now||||reg||1
